                                          2111  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2112  #
                                          2113  #  vCPU extension functions (for acceleration and compaction) follow below.
                                          2114  #
                                          2115  #  The naming convention is: SYS_<CamelCase>[_v<V>]_<N>
                                          2116  #
                                          2117  #  With <N> the maximum number of cycles the function will run
                                          2118  #  (counted from NEXT to NEXT). This is the same number that must
                                          2119  #  be passed to the 'SYS' vCPU instruction as operand, and it will
                                          2120  #  appear in the GCL code upon use.
                                          2121  #
                                          2122  #  If a SYS extension got introduced after ROM v1, the version number of
                                          2123  #  introduction is included in the name. This helps the programmer to be
                                          2124  #  reminded to verify the acutal ROM version and fail gracefully on older
                                          2125  #  ROMs than required. See also Docs/GT1-files.txt on using [romType].
                                          2126  #
                                          2127  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2128
